-- The CM curve of the proof and the scale of derivatives: the ring of
-- integers 𝓞_K of K = ℚ(√−d) inside ℂ, period lattices with their
-- Weierstrass function ℘ and invariant g₂, CM data (the source's
-- CMLattice), their area and conjugates, the Chowla–Selberg unit; the
-- number s₀, an f-th root of χ_f(α)⁻¹, and the scale per = s₁(2π/√d)^{1/2}/Ω₀.
-- Source: grh-compact/src/New/Curve/PeriodDefs.lean ("The number s₀, an
-- f-th root of chiFin(α)⁻¹, and its absolute value. Names for the curve,
-- its period and the scale of derivatives."; Parameters.vacuumRoot,
-- norm_gal_vacuumRoot, cmCurve, Ω₀, areaScale, periodFactor, jetScale),
-- with Lib/CM/Sigma/CurveTheta.lean (quadGen, quadInt, CMLattice,
-- CMLattice.latticeModule), Lib/CM/Sigma/SigmaFunction.lean
-- (PeriodPair.area), Lib/CM/MainTheorem/ConjugateCurve.lean
-- (exists_galConjugate, galConjugate), Lib/CM/FormalGroup/FormalHeight.lean
-- (CMLattice.chowla_selberg), Lib/Weil/Construction/FiniteMultiplier.lean
-- (chiAdelic, chiFin). Set-up for this proof: records of the data and
-- parameters of this proof, names for its objects.
-- Encoding. The source chooses the curve 𝓔 = ℂ/Ω₀𝓞_K
-- (Parameters.cmCurve, Parameters.Ω₀, from
-- QuadField.exists_latticeModule_eq_scaledIdeal), the unit u₀ of
-- CMLattice.chowla_selberg, and, with the Weil data of E
-- (WeilDataOfE.lean, instWeilDataE), a splitting character υ of the
-- ideles of E for each s. Here these choices are the fields of a record
-- Z (`PeriodChoice`) bound by PeriodChoiceOf, exactly the properties they
-- are chosen by; the admissible data carry one such record (the field
-- `period` of DataRecord). The conjugate curve C^σ of the source
-- (galConjugate, chosen with a₁(C^σ) = σ(a₁(C))) enters only through its
-- area, which is that of every CM datum with this a₁ (the lattice is
-- fixed by g₂ = a₁⁴/12 − 4 and g₃); the condition is stated for every
-- such datum. A period pair is the record of its two generators.
-- Part of the GRH blueprint (layer 5, the argument).
